From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:28:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Share annotation narrow replica inventories across
 origin scopes

The display holder gave every origin its own raw replica reader and semantic
inventory, repeating identical O(N) work across eight scopes. Share a bounded
path-level inventory, serialize raw/token snapshot acquisition, and carry only
64 generations of changed keys (not historical token maps). Lagging scope
selectors union retained changes; gaps, rebuilt file/connection generations,
errors and reset conservatively rebuild. Skip the sequence scan only when the
same fenced connection has unchanged data_version and total_changes.

Strict readers, exact renewal, publication and the 10s/20s bounds are unchanged.
This is a measured partial CPU reduction, NOT completion of t_3fe574bcd5c5dd01.

Proof: eight-scope decode RED16 vs2; unchanged SQL-scan RED; 28 consumer files,
371 tests green before final history-boundary parameterization; focused9 green.
Last-delta-only history mutant killed. Full scripts/check passes.
Diagnostic eight-key board/shadow-churn replay (150 windows per tier) improves
small/large mean44.063/203.664ms to13.320/38.757ms. With420256512-byte WAL:
13.739/36.480ms. Zero liveness-only key moves; scale ratios2.91/2.66 still FAIL
1.5x. Only default seeded linked rows; not full-holder acceptance. Last deployed
P1 remains25.7823% holder and0.343916% poll; no budget or renewal waiver.
